  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilience and Restoration - Hurricane Maria (DDRRF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project consists of the following:
(a) Infrastructure Works: reconstruction of Morne Jaune Primary and rehabilitation/upgrade of Delices Primary, Grand Bay Primary, Salisbury Primary and W. S. Stevens Primary.
(b) Equipment, Tools, Materials and Supplies: supply and installation of furniture, equipment/tools, information and communication technology (ICT) equipment and pedagogical materials for project schools.
(c) Design and Engineering Services: consultancy services for design, technical specifications, inspection, construction supervision and contract administration for Climate Risk Vulnerability Assessments (CRVA) and Model Safe School Programme (MSSP) assessment for the reconstructed and upgraded schools.
(d) Capacity-Building and Institutional Strengthening comprising:
(i) training in basic skill areas for community members, including women;
(ii) climate resilience construction best practices and gender sensitisation for contractors and suppliers;
(iii) basic school maintenance planning and practice for five school/community maintenance teams (SCMTs);
(iv) training in the integration of ICT in teaching climate resilient curriculum&apos; for 80 teachers and principals;
(v) preparation of a gender-responsive, climate resilient education sector plan (ESP); and
(vi) training/gender sensitisation of the Project Implementation Unit (PIU) staff. (e) Caribbean Catastrophe Risk Insurance Facility (CCRIF) premiums for parametric risk insurance for 2018 and 2019.
(f) Engagement of project management staff for PIU, a procurement consultant and an auditor to provide independent annual audits.</narrative>
  </description>
